From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iggy <iggy@triform.ai>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cloud-browser: expose embedder hook for HostFrameSinkManager
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a CONTENT_EXPORT free function in content/public/browser/
content_browser_client.h that returns the active viz::HostFrameSink
Manager*, wrapping the content-internal content::GetHostFrameSink
Manager() (defined in content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.cc).

Why this patch exists:
- Our cloud-browser worker (//cloud-browser/capture/build-integration/
  cb_devtools_agent.cc — Track E) needs to call HostFrameSinkManager
  ::CreateVideoCapturer() so the Cb.startFrameSinkCapture CDP command
  can hand a producer-side mojo::Remote to a CloudBrowserFrameSinkCapturer
  and validate the T55 capture path at runtime.
- content::GetHostFrameSinkManager() is currently only declared in
  content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h, which lives in the
  content/browser/ private include tree.
- //content/browser:browser's gn visibility list is restricted to
  //content/public/browser:browser_sources and content's own internal
  fuzzer/test targets — out-of-tree consumers (//cloud-browser:embedder)
  cannot depend on it directly. Without an exposure patch, gn check
  passes (we mark our internal include with //nogncheck) but the link
  step fails with an unresolved-symbol error for content::GetHostFrame
  SinkManager.
- A CONTENT_EXPORT free function in content/public/browser/ is the
  same shape patch 0001 used for GetEmbedderWebRtcVideoEncoderFactory
  — a stable, exported call site for embedders that funnels into the
  content-internal symbol.

Why not avoid the patch:
- Public APIs that *don't* require this patch (RenderWidgetHostView::
  CreateVideoCapturer) return std::unique_ptr<viz::ClientFrameSinkVideo
  Capturer>, a viz-crash-resilient wrapper. Our CloudBrowserFrameSinkCapturer
  constructor takes a raw mojo::Remote<viz::mojom::FrameSinkVideoCapturer>;
  using ClientFrameSinkVideoCapturer would require either refactoring our
  capturer's constructor (out of Track E scope) or holding two parallel
  capturers in the agent. Going through HostFrameSinkManager keeps the
  existing API intact and the embedder code minimal.
- The other production-grade alternative (override an existing
  ContentBrowserClient virtual to push a HostFrameSinkManager into the
  embedder at startup) is heavier weight than a free-function accessor
  and would be premature for a single Track E call site.

Why a free-function wrapper (vs. widening surface_utils.h's visibility):
- Loosening //content/browser:browser visibility to admit
  //cloud-browser:embedder leaks the entire content/browser/ private
  surface to us, not just GetHostFrameSinkManager. A targeted CONTENT_
  EXPORT shim is the narrower seam.
- Same reasoning as patch 0001 §"Why a free-function wrapper".

Embedder-side update required after this patch lands:
- capture/build-integration/cb_devtools_agent.cc currently includes
  "content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h" (with //nogncheck) and
  calls content::GetHostFrameSinkManager() directly. With this patch
  in place that include + call should be retired in favor of
  content::GetEmbedderHostFrameSinkManager() — a one-line rename in
  the embedder, plus dropping the //nogncheck. Done in a follow-up
  embedder commit, not in this patch (which is chromium-only).

Upstream considerations:
- Upstream chromium does not currently expose HostFrameSinkManager via
  a public header. Chromium's own non-content embedders (cast_shell,
  weblayer, headless) use chromium-internal access either by being in-
  tree or via separate carve-outs. If our embedder pattern proves
  durable across two roll cycles, file an upstream bug to expose this
  via content/public/browser/ proper — the shape would mirror this
  patch.

Touched files:
- content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h  (forward decl,
                                                     CONTENT_EXPORT free
                                                     function decl)
- content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc (free function impl,
                                                     surface_utils.h
                                                     include)

Resolved against branch-heads/7727 (Chromium 147 stable). Context lines
are illustrative; the patch is shape-only until first build apply, per
patches/README.md §"shape-only". Conflicts on rebase are fix-forward.
---
 content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h  | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc b/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc
index 5c72f6a34e..a5b1c2d0e1 100644
--- a/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.cc
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 #include "components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.h"
 #include "components/viz/common/features.h"
+#include "components/viz/host/host_frame_sink_manager.h"
+#include "content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h"
 #include "content/browser/ai/echo_ai_manager_impl.h"
 #include "content/browser/cpu_performance/cpu_performance.h"
 #include "content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.h"
@@ -976,6 +978,18 @@ GetEmbedderWebRtcVideoEncoderFactory() {
   return browser_client->GetWebRtcVideoEncoderFactory();
 }

+viz::HostFrameSinkManager* GetEmbedderHostFrameSinkManager() {
+  // content::GetHostFrameSinkManager() is declared in
+  // content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h, which is intentionally
+  // private to content/browser/. This wrapper lives inside the content
+  // library (CONTENT_IMPLEMENTATION is defined here) and re-exports the
+  // accessor as CONTENT_EXPORT so out-of-tree embedders (//cloud-browser:
+  // embedder consuming this through //content/public/browser) can reach
+  // the host without depending on //content/browser:browser, whose
+  // visibility list rejects out-of-tree consumers.
+  return content::GetHostFrameSinkManager();
+}
+
 std::unique_ptr<ui::SelectFilePolicy>
 ContentBrowserClient::CreateSelectFilePolicy(WebContents* web_contents) {
   return nullptr;
diff --git a/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h b/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h
index 9052f617e1..b7c95e1d8a 100644
--- a/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h
+++ b/content/public/browser/content_browser_client.h
@@ -181,6 +181,10 @@ namespace webrtc {
 class VideoEncoderFactory;
 }  // namespace webrtc

+namespace viz {
+class HostFrameSinkManager;
+}  // namespace viz
+
 namespace optimization_guide {
 class ModelBrokerClient;
 }  // namespace optimization_guide
@@ -3469,6 +3473,16 @@ class CONTENT_EXPORT ContentBrowserClient {
 CONTENT_EXPORT std::unique_ptr<webrtc::VideoEncoderFactory>
 GetEmbedderWebRtcVideoEncoderFactory();

+// Returns the active viz::HostFrameSinkManager*, or nullptr if none is
+// available (e.g. between BrowserMainLoop teardown and process exit).
+// Lives in content/public/browser so out-of-tree embedders can reach
+// the host without depending on //content/browser:browser, which has
+// a restrictive visibility list. Funnels through the content-internal
+// content::GetHostFrameSinkManager() declared in
+// content/browser/compositor/surface_utils.h. See patch 0005.
+CONTENT_EXPORT viz::HostFrameSinkManager*
+GetEmbedderHostFrameSinkManager();
+
 }  // namespace content

 #endif  // CONTENT_PUBLIC_BROWSER_CONTENT_BROWSER_CLIENT_H_
--
2.43.0

